(>> 6.1 Transducer Classification and Performance Metrics) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A transducer is a device that converts physical or biochemical parameters \(temperature,) Tj
T*
(pressure, pH, analyte concentration\) into measurable electrical signals.) Tj
T*
(* Classification Schemes:) Tj
T*
(1. Active vs. Passive: Active transducers generate an electrical signal directly from) Tj
T*
(the measured physical energy without requiring an external excitation power supply) Tj
T*
(\(e.g., Thermocouple [Seebeck effect], Piezoelectric sensor, Photovoltaic cell\). Passive) Tj
T*
(transducers require an external excitation voltage/current to measure resistance,) Tj
T*
(inductance, or capacitance variations \(e.g., RTD, Strain gauge, Thermistor, LVDT\).) Tj
T*
(2. Primary vs. Secondary: Primary transducer converts physical input into a mechanical) Tj
T*
(displacement \(e.g., Bourdon tube, Diaphragm\). Secondary transducer converts mechanical) Tj
T*
(displacement into electrical output \(e.g., LVDT attached to Bourdon tube\).) Tj
T*
(* Transducer Characteristics: Sensitivity \(S = Delta V / Delta Physical_Input\),) Tj
T*
(Linearity, Accuracy, Precision, Resolution, Hysteresis, and Response Time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.2 Temperature, Pressure and Displacement Sensors) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Resistance Temperature Detectors \(RTD\): Positive temperature coefficient \(PTC\)) Tj
T*
(metal sensor. Resistance relationship: R_T = R_0 * [ 1 + alpha * \(T - T_0\) ]. Pt100) Tj
T*
(is the industrial gold standard \(Platinum, R_0 = 100 Omega at 0 deg C, alpha =) Tj
T*
(0.00385 / deg C\). Highly linear, stable, and accurate across -200 deg C to +650 deg) Tj
T*
(C.) Tj
T*
(* Thermocouples: Based on the Seebeck Effect: when two dissimilar metals \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(Copper and Constantan [Type T], Chromel and Alumel [Type K]\) are joined at two) Tj
T*
(junctions held at different temperatures \(T_hot and T_cold\), a net thermoelectric EMF) Tj
T*
(is produced: V_emf = alpha_Seebeck * \(T_hot - T_cold\). Operates across extreme) Tj
T*
(temperature ranges \(-270 deg C to +1,800 deg C\).) Tj
T*
(* Strain Gauge: Piezoresistive sensor whose electrical resistance changes under) Tj
T*
(mechanical strain. Gauge Factor \(GF\): GF = \(Delta R / R\) / \(Delta L / L\) = \(Delta R /) Tj
T*
(R\) / epsilon = 1 + 2*nu + \(Delta rho / rho\) / epsilon. For metal foil gauges, GF ~) Tj
T*
(2.0. Interfaced via a Wheatstone Bridge circuit.) Tj
T*
(* Linear Variable Differential Transformer \(LVDT\): Inductive displacement transducer) Tj
T*
(consisting of one primary coil excited by AC voltage \(1-10 kHz\) and two identical) Tj
T*
(secondary coils wound symmetrically in series opposition. A movable ferromagnetic) Tj
T*
(core alters flux coupling: when centered \(null position\), induced voltages cancel:) Tj
T*
(V_out = V_s1 - V_s2 = 0. Displacement moves core closer to one secondary, producing) Tj
T*
(an AC output whose amplitude is proportional to displacement and phase indicates) Tj
T*
(direction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

