(* Biosensor Architecture: Integrates a biological recognition element \(enzymes,) Tj
T*
(antibodies, nucleic acids, whole cells\) in intimate contact with a physicochemical) Tj
T*
(transducer \(electrochemical, optical, piezoelectric, thermal\).) Tj
T*
(* Glucose Biosensor \(Clark-Type Amperometric Electrode\): Utilizes Glucose Oxidase) Tj
T*
(\(GOx\) immobilized on an electrode surface:) Tj
T*
(Glucose + O2 + H2O --[GOx]--> Gluconic Acid + H2O2.) Tj
T*
(H2O2 is oxidized at a platinum anode held at +0.6 V vs. Ag/AgCl: H2O2 -> O2 + 2 H+ + 2) Tj
T*
(e-.) Tj
T*
(The resulting anodic current is directly proportional to glucose concentration in the) Tj
T*
(biological fluid.) Tj
