([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Industrial RTD \(Pt100\) Resistance and Temperature Measurement]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A platinum RTD \(Pt100\) has a resistance of R_0 = 100.0 Omega at 0 deg C and) Tj
T*
(temperature coefficient alpha = 0.00385 / deg C. Calculate: \(1\) Resistance at bioreactor) Tj
T*
(operating temperature T = 37.0 deg C, \(2\) If measured resistance in an autoclave is R_T) Tj
T*
(= 146.2 Omega, determine the autoclave temperature.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Resistance at 37 deg C:) Tj
T*
(Formula: R_T = R_0 * [ 1 + alpha * \(T - 0\) ].) Tj
T*
(R_37 = 100.0 * [ 1 + 0.00385 * 37.0 ] = 100.0 * [ 1 + 0.14245 ] = 100.0 * 1.14245 =) Tj
T*
(114.25 Omega.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Determine Autoclave Temperature from R_T = 146.2 Omega:) Tj
T*
(146.2 = 100.0 * [ 1 + 0.00385 * T ].) Tj
T*
(1.462 = 1 + 0.00385 * T => 0.00385 * T = 0.462.) Tj
T*
(T = 0.462 / 0.00385 = 120.0 deg C.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: The measured resistance corresponds exactly to 120 deg C, confirming) Tj
T*
