([SOLVED PROBLEM 2: Wheatstone Bridge Strain Gauge Circuit Sensitivity]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A metallic strain gauge with nominal resistance R = 120 Omega and Gauge Factor) Tj
T*
(GF = 2.0 is mounted on a steel biomechanical implant arm. The gauge forms one active arm) Tj
T*
(of a balanced Wheatstone bridge excited by V_s = 10 V DC. If mechanical load creates a) Tj
T*
(tensile strain of epsilon = 500 micro-strain \(500 * 10^-6\), calculate: \(1\) Change in) Tj
T*
(resistance Delta R, \(2\) Bridge output voltage Delta V_out.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Resistance Change Delta R:) Tj
T*
(GF = \(Delta R / R\) / epsilon => Delta R = GF * epsilon * R) Tj
T*
(Delta R = 2.0 * \(500 * 10^-6\) * 120 Omega = 1000 * 10^-6 * 120 = 0.120 Omega.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Bridge Output Voltage for Quarter-Bridge Configuration:) Tj
T*
(For a quarter-bridge where Delta R << R:) Tj
T*
(Delta V_out = \(V_s / 4\) * \(Delta R / R\) = \(V_s / 4\) * GF * epsilon) Tj
T*
(Delta V_out = \(10 V / 4\) * \(0.120 / 120\) = 2.5 V * 0.0010 = 0.0025 Volts = 2.5 mV.) Tj
T*
(Signal Conditioning Requirement: A differential instrumentation amplifier with gain A_v) Tj
T*
(= 1000 is required to scale this 2.5 mV signal to a 2.5 V level for microcontroller ADC) Tj
T*
(digitization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 3: Microcontroller 10-Bit ADC Resolution and Quantization]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: An embedded biotechnology data logger uses a microcontroller with a 10-bit) Tj
T*
(Successive Approximation ADC powered by a reference voltage V_ref = 3.30 V. Calculate:) Tj
T*
(\(1\) Number of discrete quantization levels, \(2\) Voltage resolution per Least Significant) Tj
T*
(Bit \(LSB\), \(3\) Digital output code for an analog biosensor voltage input of V_in = 1.65) Tj
T*
(V, \(4\) Quantization error.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Discrete Quantization Levels:) Tj
T*
(For an n-bit ADC: Total levels = 2^n = 2^10 = 1,024 levels \(codes 0 to 1,023\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Voltage Resolution \(LSB Size\):) Tj
T*
(Resolution = V_ref / 2^n = 3.30 V / 1,024 = 0.0032226 Volts = 3.223 mV/LSB.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Digital Output Code for V_in = 1.65 V:) Tj
T*
(Digital Code D = floor\( \(V_in / V_ref\) * 2^n \) = floor\( \(1.65 / 3.30\) * 1,024 \) = floor\() Tj
T*
(0.5 * 1024 \) = 512.) Tj
T*
(In Binary: 512 = \(10 0000 0000\)_2; In Hexadecimal: 0x200.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Quantization Error:) Tj
T*
(Maximum quantization uncertainty = +/- 0.5 LSB = +/- 0.5 * 3.223 mV = +/- 1.61 mV.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
