(Problem: An LVDT displacement sensor has an output of 2.0 V RMS when its core is) Tj
T*
(displaced by 5.0 mm from its null position. Calculate: \(1\) Sensitivity of the LVDT in) Tj
T*
(V/mm and V/micrometer, \(2\) Core displacement when the output voltage reads 0.8 V RMS.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Sensitivity S:) Tj
T*
(S = Delta V_out / Delta x = 2.0 V / 5.0 mm = 0.40 V/mm \(400 mV/mm\).) Tj
T*
(In V/micrometer: S = 0.40 V / 1000 micrometers = 0.0004 V/micrometer = 0.40) Tj
T*
(mV/micrometer.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Displacement for V_out = 0.8 V:) Tj
T*
(Delta x = V_out / S = 0.8 V / \(0.40 V/mm\) = 2.0 mm \(2,000 micrometers\).) Tj
T*
