/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.5 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Explain the construction, working principle, and differential voltage) Tj
T*
(cancellation of an LVDT.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Construction: An LVDT consists of a hollow non-magnetic cylindrical former. A) Tj
T*
(single primary winding P is wound at the center, excited by an AC carrier voltage \(1-10) Tj
T*
(kHz, 3-15V\). Two identical secondary windings S1 and S2 are wound symmetrically on) Tj
T*
(either side of the primary and connected in series opposition. A high-permeability) Tj
T*
(nickel-iron core moves axially inside the former. Working Principle: When the core is at) Tj
T*
(the central null position, flux linking S1 and S2 is identical, inducing equal voltages) Tj
T*
(E_s1 = E_s2. The net output is V_out = E_s1 - E_s2 = 0. When the core moves toward S1,) Tj
T*
(magnetic coupling to S1 increases while coupling to S2 decreases \(E_s1 > E_s2\),) Tj
T*
(producing a net output voltage in phase with primary excitation. When the core moves) Tj
T*
(toward S2, E_s2 > E_s1, producing an output voltage 180 degrees out of phase. Output) Tj
T*
(magnitude is linearly proportional to displacement over its operating range.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Diagram and describe the architecture and biochemical sensing mechanism of an) Tj
T*
(amperometric Glucose Biosensor.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Architecture: A Clark-type amperometric glucose biosensor comprises a) Tj
T*
(three-electrode electrochemical cell: a Platinum working electrode, a Silver/Silver) Tj
T*
(Chloride \(Ag/AgCl\) reference electrode, and a Platinum auxiliary electrode, enclosed) Tj
T*
(behind an outer semi-permeable polycarbonate membrane and an inner enzyme membrane.) Tj
T*
(Biochemical mechanism: Glucose Oxidase \(GOx\) containing flavin adenine dinucleotide) Tj
T*
(\(FAD\) is covalently immobilized on the working electrode. When glucose diffuses through) Tj
T*
(the membrane, GOx catalyzes its oxidation: Glucose + O2 + H2O -> Gluconic Acid + H2O2.) Tj
T*
(The working electrode is biased at +0.6V relative to Ag/AgCl. At this potential, H2O2) Tj
T*
(undergoes electrocatalytic oxidation at the platinum anode: H2O2 -> O2 + 2 H+ + 2 e-.) Tj
T*
(The resulting anodic electron current is directly proportional to the enzymatic) Tj
T*
(production rate of H2O2, which in turn is linearly proportional to blood glucose) Tj
T*
(concentration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
